  "body": "Positioned just moments from the golden sands of Milford Beach, 12 Beach Road offers an exceptional combination of masonry construction, architectural design and coastal lifestyle. Built in 2012 and awarded a Master Builders Gold Award in 2013, this is a home where quality is immediately apparent. \r\n\r\nThe location is a major part of the appeal. A short walk across the pedestrian bridge connects you directly to Milford Reserve and the beach, making morning swims, paddleboarding, coastal walks or simply enjoying time by the water part of everyday life. Milford Village, its cafés, restaurants and amenities are also within easy reach.\r\n\r\nLiving is positioned on the ground floor, where a kitchen with butler’s pantry sits at the heart of the home. Open-plan dining and family living flow effortlessly to two separate outdoor entertaining areas, creating a home that works equally well for relaxed everyday living or entertaining. A separate media room provides a second living space, while the dedicated office is ideal for those working from home.\r\n\r\nUpstairs are four bedrooms, all benefiting from the home’s elevated position. The master suite is particularly impressive, enjoying gorgeous views across the reserve towards the water, complemented by a generous walk-in wardrobe and ensuite. In our opinion, the scale and layout will have particular appeal to a small family, professional couple or downsizers wanting quality, privacy and space without excessive maintenance.\r\n\r\nDouble internal-access garaging with secure additional parking behind electronic gates, while concealed storage provides plenty of room for bikes, kayaks, paddleboards and all the equipment that comes with living this close to the beach.\r\n\r\nZoned for Campbells Bay Primary, Murrays Bay Intermediate and both Westlake Boys’ and Girls’ High Schools, this is an exceptional offering in one of Milford’s most desirable locations.\r\n\r\nIf you can't reach Andrew Dorreen, please contact his Sales Associate, Anna Jones, on 021 489 171",
